-- test/fixtures/3.6.0-start-calls.lua
-- The engine calls a fresh Strata 3.6.0 sends: init, the start-up
-- coroutine (test/helpers.lua's finish_startup), then every voice started
-- with toggle_voice in voice order and every voice stopped the same way,
-- every v<i>_buf_scan at 0 (3.6.0's default, asserted while recording).
-- test/unit/system_37_test.lua compares 3.7's calls for the same steps with
-- this list (design §12, the 3.7 plan's Task 3a).
--
-- How it was recorded (2026-11-16): a temporary detached worktree of the tag
-- v3.6.0 (`git worktree add --detach <scratch>/v360 v3.6.0`), a throwaway
-- unit file there that seeds math.randomseed(37), runs h.load_strata(),
-- h.finish_startup(context) and the starts and stops above, and writes each
-- of context.engine_calls as `name(args)`, numbers with "%.9g" and strings
-- with "%q"; run with `lua test/run.lua <its filter>` (Lua 5.3.6), and the
-- worktree then removed with `git worktree remove`. Each run of consecutive
-- setVoiceParam calls on one voice comes in a pairs() order that changes
-- from run to run, so the test sorts each such run on both sides before it
-- compares; nothing else is reordered. 3.6.0 sends no setDelay at a start.
